\ Spitfire: the guns, from first principles. Each gun fires its published
\ rounds a minute at its published muzzle velocity; a frame's rounds from
\ one group of guns fly together as a salvo, from the gun with the
\ shooter's velocity added, falling under gravity (the air's drag left out).
\ A salvo spreads in a cone: the Spitfire's guns, harmonised on one point
\ 250 yards ahead, put a cone 6 ft across at 200 yards (published), taken
\ as four standard deviations, 0.0025 rad; the Bf 110's nose guns, close
\ together and parallel, are given the same; a rear gunner's MG 15 on its
\ moving mount aims to within 0.01 rad (an estimate). The target is a disc
\ of the area it presents along the line of fire: its frontal, wing and side
\ areas, each in proportion to how squarely it faces the salvo (the wing
\ areas published, the frontal and side areas measured from the models).
\ A salvo passing the disc's centre at b, spread s at that distance, disc
\ radius a, lands the share a² ÷ (a² + 2s²) × e^(−b² ÷ (a² + 2s²)) of its
\ rounds: a round Gaussian spread falling on a round soft-edged target.
\
\ A rifle-calibre round's hit counts 1 and a 20 mm shell's 22.2, from the
\ rule that a single-engined fighter falls to about 100 rifle-calibre hits
\ or 4 to 5 of 20 mm. An aircraft falls when its hits reach its strength,
\ 100 × (empty mass ÷ 2,184 kg)^0.7396: the fighter's 100 at the Spitfire's
\ empty mass, and the B-17's 20 hits of 20 mm, the German figure, at its
\ 16,391 kg. The Bf 110 C (4,500 kg) takes 171, the He 111 (6,900 kg) 234,
\ the Ju 88 (8,050 kg, the A-4's) 263. The air-firing exercise's Lysander
\ tug (1,887 kg, 24.15 m² of wing, published; its frontal and side areas
\ estimates) and drogue (estimates) count their hits and never fall. The
\ player's aircraft takes its
\ hits as damage, 100 stopping the engine; a round hit holes the radiator
\ 4.3% of the time and the oil cooler 1.5%, their shares of the frontal
\ area (estimates from the model).
\
\ The guns and their rounds: the Spitfire's eight Brownings, 1,150 rounds a
\ minute at 811 m/s, 300 each; the Hurricane's eight, the inner pairs' 334
\ rounds and the outer pairs' 287 taken as 310.5 each, its empty mass
\ (2,260 kg) and presented areas estimates; the Bf 110's four MG 17s, 1,100 at 895 m/s,
\ 1,000 each, two MG FF, 530 at 600 m/s, 180 each, and its rear MG 15; the
\ bombers' rear MG 15, 1,025 at 755 m/s from 75-round drums, 4 s to change
\ a drum (an estimate). Computer-flown shooters fire when their aim, with
\ the lead and drop their rounds need, puts the target within the spread,
\ inside 600 m (an estimate), the raid's gunners after 3 s to take aim
\ (an estimate); whether they hit is the salvo's flight alone.
\
\ The battle shows: each salvo a tracer streak; each hit a flash; an
\ aircraft past half its strength trails smoke, past three quarters fire;
\ and an aircraft in air colder than -40 °C leaves a contrail.

0xffe070 constant tracer-colour
0xff7050 constant german-tracer-colour
22.2 constant cannon-weight
0.0025 constant fixed-spread
0.01 constant rear-spread
600 constant opening-range
3 constant gunner-aim-time
4 constant drum-change-time
1.5 constant salvo-life
0.043 constant radiator-share
0.015 constant oil-cooler-share
20 cannon-weight * 100 / ln 16391 2184 / ln / constant strength-exponent

\ each type's guns, in groups that fire together: how many, rounds a minute, muzzle velocity, the weight of a hit, the spread, rounds each (or in a drum), fixed forward or the rear gunner's
variable gun-table
{ :spitfire [ { :guns 8 :rate 1150 :velocity 811 :weight 1 :spread fixed-spread :rounds 300 :mount :fixed } ]
  :hurricane [ { :guns 8 :rate 1150 :velocity 811 :weight 1 :spread fixed-spread :rounds 310.5 :mount :fixed } ]
  :bf-110 [ { :guns 4 :rate 1100 :velocity 895 :weight 1 :spread fixed-spread :rounds 1000 :mount :fixed }
            { :guns 2 :rate 530 :velocity 600 :weight cannon-weight :spread fixed-spread :rounds 180 :mount :fixed }
            { :guns 1 :rate 1025 :velocity 755 :weight 1 :spread rear-spread :rounds 75 :mount :rear } ]
  :he-111 [ { :guns 1 :rate 1025 :velocity 755 :weight 1 :spread rear-spread :rounds 75 :mount :rear } ]
  :ju-88 [ { :guns 1 :rate 1025 :velocity 755 :weight 1 :spread rear-spread :rounds 75 :mount :rear } ] } to gun-table

\ each type's empty mass, kg, and the areas it presents, m²: from ahead, from above (the wing's published area) and from the side
variable aircraft-figures
{ :spitfire { :empty 2184 :frontal 3.7 :planform 22.48 :side 7.5 }
  :hurricane { :empty 2260 :frontal 4.2 :planform 23.92 :side 9.5 }
  :bf-110 { :empty 4500 :frontal 7.9 :planform 38.5 :side 14 }
  :he-111 { :empty 6900 :frontal 14.9 :planform 87.6 :side 30 }
  :ju-88 { :empty 8050 :frontal 12.3 :planform 54.7 :side 26 }
  :lysander { :empty 1887 :frontal 4.5 :planform 24.15 :side 11 }
  :drogue { :empty 2184 :frontal 0.79 :planform 5.1 :side 5.1 } } to aircraft-figures

\ the salvos in flight, and the flashes of hits, each [ position age ]
variable salvos
[ ] to salvos
variable flashes
[ ] to flashes
0.12 constant flash-life
0xfff0a0 constant flash-colour
0xff9030 constant fire-colour

\ the salvos and flashes forgotten, for a new flight
: reset-gunnery ( -- )
	| ^salvos ^flashes |
	[ ] to salvos
	[ ] to flashes ;

\ whether an aircraft is the player's, and its type
: player? ( craft -- flag ) :kind null @or null? ;
: kind-of ( craft -- kind )
	| craft |
	craft player? if craft@type@kind exit then
	craft :kind :spitfire @or ;

\ an aircraft's velocity: the player's its own, the others' from their attitude and speed
: velocity-of ( craft -- velocity )
	| craft |
	craft player? if craft@velocity exit then
	craft craft-velocity ;

\ whether an aircraft can still be hit: the player's until it crashes, the others while flying
: hittable? ( craft -- flag )
	| craft |
	craft player? if plane@crashed not exit then
	craft flying? ;

\ the hits that bring a type down, in rifle-calibre rounds
: strength ( kind -- hits )
	| kind |
	aircraft-figures kind @ to figures
	figures@empty 2184 / strength-exponent ^ 100 * ;

\ the radius of the disc an aircraft presents to a point
: presented-radius ( target from -- radius )
	| target from |
	aircraft-figures target kind-of @ to figures
	target@position from v- v-unit to sight
	target@attitude to attitude
	figures@frontal attitude@forward sight v-dot abs *
	figures@planform attitude@up sight v-dot abs * +
	figures@side attitude@right sight v-dot abs * +
	PI / sqrt ;

\ how the squadron names an aircraft it shot down
: kind-name ( kind -- text )
	| kind |
	kind :bf-110 = if "A BF 110" exit then
	kind :he-111 = if "AN HE 111" exit then
	"A JU 88" ;

\ an aircraft's rounds left in each group, its rear gunner's drum change and aim still to come, set from its type the first time asked
: rounds-left ( craft -- rounds )
	| craft |
	craft :rounds-left null @or to rounds
	rounds null? not if rounds exit then
	gun-table craft kind-of @ ( group | group@mount :rear = if group@rounds else group@rounds group@guns * then ) map to rounds
	rounds craft!rounds-left
	0 craft!reload-left
	gunner-aim-time craft!aim-left
	rounds ;

\ where to aim to hit a target with rounds of a muzzle velocity: where it will be when they arrive, moved as the shooter's velocity carries them, and above it by their drop
: lead-point ( shooter target muzzle-velocity -- point )
	| shooter target muzzle-velocity |
	target@position shooter@position v- v-length muzzle-velocity / to flight-time
	target velocity-of shooter velocity-of v- flight-time v* target@position v+
	[ 0 gravity flight-time sq * 2 / 0 ] v+ ;

\ a frame's rounds from one group of a shooter's guns, a salvo along a direction at a target: rounds spent from the group's store, the player's from its seconds of fire
: fire-group ( shooter index direction target credit source dt -- )
	| shooter index direction target credit source dt |
	gun-table shooter kind-of @ index @i to group
	group@guns group@rate * 60 / dt * to rounds
	shooter player? not if
		shooter rounds-left to store
		rounds store index @i min2 to rounds
		store store index @i rounds - index !i drop
	then
	rounds 0 <= if exit then
	salvos
	{ :position shooter@position direction 4 v* v+
	  :velocity shooter velocity-of direction group@velocity v* v+
	  :rounds rounds :weight group@weight :spread group@spread :travel 0 :age 0
	  :target target :credit credit :source source }
	add-last! drop ;

\ of some aircraft, the one nearest a shooter's line of fire, ahead of it within 1,200 m, or null
: nearest-on-line ( shooter candidates -- target )
	| shooter candidates |
	candidates ( craft |
		shooter craft@position bearing-from drop to ahead
		craft hittable? ahead 0 > and ahead 1200 < and
	) filter to ahead-of
	ahead-of size 0 = if null exit then
	ahead-of ( craft | shooter craft@position bearing-from swap drop ) sort-by first ;

\ whether a shooter's fixed guns bear on a target: within the opening range, the lead point within the spread and the target's disc of the line of fire
: guns-bear? ( shooter target group -- flag )
	| shooter target group |
	shooter target group@velocity lead-point to aim
	aim shooter@position v- v-length to range
	range opening-range > if false exit then
	shooter aim bearing-from to off-line to ahead
	ahead 0 > off-line group@spread 2 * target shooter@position presented-radius range 1 max2 / + < and ;

\ hits on an aircraft: the player's takes them as damage, with leaks from the radiator's and the oil cooler's shares of the rounds and what hit it named; another falls when its hits reach its strength, the player's kills counted
: apply-hits ( target hit-rounds weight credit source -- )
	| target hit-rounds weight credit source |
	hit-rounds weight * to weighted
	target player? if
		plane@damage weighted + 100 min2 plane!damage
		source say
		1 1 radiator-share - hit-rounds ^ - random > if
			plane@coolant-leak 0.01 + plane!coolant-leak
			"HIT IN THE RADIATOR  -  GLYCOL LEAKING, WATCH THE TEMPERATURE" say
		then
		1 1 oil-cooler-share - hit-rounds ^ - random > if
			plane@oil-leak 0.005 + plane!oil-leak
			"HIT IN THE OIL SYSTEM  -  WATCH THE OIL PRESSURE" say
		then
		exit
	then
	target@hits weighted + target!hits
	weighted 1 >= if flashes [ target@position 0 ] add-last! drop then
	target practice-target? if exit then
	target@hits target kind-of strength < if exit then
	target flying? not if exit then
	:falling target!state
	target :role :bomber @or :spitfire = if "A SPITFIRE IS GOING DOWN" say exit then
	credit :player = if
		:kills game@ 1+ :kills game!
		"RAIDER DESTROYED" say
		exit
	then
	target@kind kind-name "A SPITFIRE HAS SHOT DOWN {0}" format say ;

\ one salvo's step: it flies and falls; if its target is in its reach, at the step where it passes nearest, the share of its rounds that hit are spent on it
: move-salvo ( salvo dt -- )
	| salvo dt |
	salvo@position to start
	salvo@velocity [ 0 gravity dt * 0 ] v- to velocity
	start salvo@velocity velocity v+ 0.5 v* dt v* v+ to finish
	velocity salvo!velocity
	finish salvo!position
	salvo@travel finish start v- v-length + salvo!travel
	salvo@age dt + salvo!age
	salvo@target to target
	target null? if exit then
	target hittable? not if exit then
	target@position to centre
	start centre target velocity-of dt v* v- v- to near
	finish centre v- to far
	far near v- to path
	path path v-dot to path-length
	path-length 0 = if exit then
	near path v-dot negate path-length / to along
	along 0 <= along 1 > or if exit then
	near path along v* v+ v-length to miss
	salvo@spread salvo@travel * to spread
	target start presented-radius to radius
	radius sq 2 spread sq * + to width
	radius sq width / miss sq negate width / exp * to share
	salvo@rounds share * to hit-rounds
	salvo@rounds hit-rounds - salvo!rounds
	target hit-rounds salvo@weight salvo@credit salvo@source apply-hits ;

\ the salvos' step: each flies, and those older than their life or spent are dropped
: advance-salvos ( dt -- )
	| dt ^salvos |
	salvos ( salvo | salvo dt move-salvo ) each
	salvos ( salvo | salvo@age salvo :life salvo-life @or < salvo@rounds 0.01 > and ) filter to salvos ;

\ the Spitfires the raid can fire at: the player's, unless crashed, and the squadron's still flying
: spitfires ( -- crafts )
	plane@crashed if [ ] else [ plane ] then
	wingmen ( wingman | wingman flying? ) filter concat ;

\ the raid still flying
: raiders ( -- crafts ) bombers ( bomber | bomber flying? ) filter ;

\ the player's guns while the trigger is held and rounds last, at the raider nearest the line of fire
: player-fire ( dt -- )
	| dt |
	:firing game@ plane@ammunition 0 > and not if exit then
	plane@ammunition dt - 0 max2 plane!ammunition
	plane raiders nearest-on-line to target
	plane 0 plane@attitude@forward target :player "" dt fire-group ;

\ the squadron's guns: each Spitfire still flying fires when they bear on the raider nearest its line of fire
: wingmen-fire ( dt -- )
	| dt |
	raiders to targets
	wingmen ( wingman |
		wingman flying? if
			wingman targets nearest-on-line to target
			target null? not if
				gun-table :spitfire @ first to group
				wingman target group guns-bear? if
					wingman 0 wingman@attitude@forward target :wingman "" dt fire-group
				then
			then
		then
	) each ;

\ the escort's nose guns, the MG 17s and the MG FFs together, when they bear on the Spitfire nearest the line of fire; and a warning, at most every 6 s, of a Bf 110 behind the player within 800 m
: escort-fire ( dt -- )
	| dt |
	spitfires to targets
	game :tail-warning-left 0 @or dt - :tail-warning-left game!
	bombers ( fighter |
		fighter fighter? fighter@state :inbound = and if
			fighter targets nearest-on-line to target
			target null? not if
				gun-table :bf-110 @ first to group
				fighter target group guns-bear? if
					fighter 0 fighter@attitude@forward target :german "HIT BY A BF 110'S GUNS" dt fire-group
					fighter 1 fighter@attitude@forward target :german "HIT BY A BF 110'S CANNON" dt fire-group
				then
			then
			plane fighter@position bearing-from drop 0 < fighter@position plane@position v- v-length 800 < and :tail-warning-left game@ 0 <= and if
				"A BF 110 IS ON YOUR TAIL  -  BREAK" say
				6 :tail-warning-left game!
			then
		then
	) each ;

\ the rear gunners: after taking aim, each fires at the nearest Spitfire behind it within the opening range, aiming at its lead point; an empty drum is changed
: gunners-fire ( dt -- )
	| dt |
	spitfires to targets
	bombers ( gunner |
		gunner flying? gun-table gunner kind-of null @or null? not and if
			gunner rounds-left to store
			store size 1- to index
			gunner@aim-left dt - 0 max2 gunner!aim-left
			gunner@reload-left 0 > if
				gunner@reload-left dt - gunner!reload-left
				gunner@reload-left 0 <= if
					gun-table gunner kind-of @ last to drum-group
					store drum-group@rounds index !i drop
				then
			else
				targets ( craft |
					gunner craft@position bearing-from drop 0 < craft@position gunner@position v- v-length opening-range < and
				) filter ( craft | craft@position gunner@position v- v-length ) sort-by to behind
				behind size 0 > gunner@aim-left 0 <= and if
					behind first to target
					gun-table gunner kind-of @ last to group
					gunner target group@velocity lead-point gunner@position v- v-unit to direction
					gunner index direction target :german "HIT BY RETURN FIRE" dt fire-group
					store index @i 0 <= if drum-change-time gunner!reload-left then
				then
			then
		then
	) each ;

\ the damage showing: an aircraft past half its strength trails smoke, a point every 0.25 s, the last 40 kept
: trail-damage ( dt -- )
	| dt |
	bombers wingmen concat ( craft |
		craft flying? craft practice-target? not and craft@hits craft kind-of strength 0.5 * >= and if
			craft@smoke-left dt - craft!smoke-left
			craft@smoke-left 0 <= if
				craft@smoke craft@position add-last! drop
				craft@smoke size 40 > if craft@smoke 1 skip craft!smoke then
				0.25 craft!smoke-left
			then
		then
	) each ;

\ lines in the view, each [ from to ], in one colour
: draw-lines ( lines colour -- )
	| lines colour |
	lines size 0 = if exit then
	[ 0 lines size 1 do k
		lines k @i to line
		line first
		line second
	loop ] to ends
	ends ( point | point spread 1 4 array ) map flatten ends size 4 matrix to points
	[ 0 ends size 1 do k k loop ] to edges
	points camera matmul edges colour draw-edges ;

\ contrails: an aircraft in air colder than -40 °C (an estimate of where engine exhaust freezes) leaves a point every 0.5 s, each kept 60 s; the trails as [ position time ] points per aircraft, the clock running with the guns' steps
-40 constant contrail-temperature
60 constant contrail-life
variable battle-clock
0 to battle-clock

: lay-contrails ( dt -- )
	| dt ^battle-clock |
	battle-clock dt + to battle-clock
	bombers wingmen concat plane@crashed if [ ] else [ plane ] then concat ( craft |
		craft :contrail [ ] @or ( point | battle-clock point second - contrail-life < ) filter to trail
		craft hittable? craft@position second air-temperature contrail-temperature < and if
			craft :contrail-left 0 @or dt - to left
			left 0 <= if
				trail [ craft@position battle-clock ] add-last! drop
				0.5 to left
			then
			left craft!contrail-left
		then
		trail craft!contrail
	) each ;

\ the contrails as lines between each trail's points 0.5 s apart, white
: draw-contrails ( -- )
	bombers wingmen concat [ plane ] concat ( craft |
		craft :contrail [ ] @or to trail
		[ 1 trail size 1 do k
			trail k 1- @i to earlier
			trail k @i to later
			later second earlier second - 0.6 < if [ earlier first later first ] then
		loop ]
	) map [ ] ' concat reduce cloud-top-colour draw-lines ;

\ the flashes' ages, those past their life dropped
: age-flashes ( dt -- )
	| dt ^flashes |
	flashes ( flash | [ flash first flash second dt + ] ) map ( flash | flash second flash-life < ) filter to flashes ;

\ the guns' step: every shooter's guns, the salvos' flight, the flashes, the smoke of the damaged
: advance-gunnery ( dt -- )
	| dt |
	dt 0 <= if exit then
	dt player-fire
	dt wingmen-fire
	dt escort-fire
	dt gunners-fire
	dt advance-salvos
	dt age-flashes
	dt trail-damage
	dt lay-contrails ;

\ the battle's light: the salvos' tracers, a 20 m streak behind each, the Spitfires' yellow and the raid's red; each hit's flash, a star of six arms 3 m long; the fire of an aircraft past three quarters of its strength, five flickering strokes trailing up to 12 m behind it; bright by night as by day
: draw-battle ( -- )
	| ^lighting |
	draw-contrails
	lighting to scene-lighting
	1 to lighting
	flashes ( flash |
		flash first to centre
		[ [ 3 0 0 ] [ 0 3 0 ] [ 0 0 3 ] ] ( arm | [ centre arm v+ centre arm v- ] ) map
	) map [ ] ' concat reduce to flash-lines
	flash-lines flash-colour draw-lines
	bombers wingmen concat ( craft |
		craft flying? craft practice-target? not and craft@hits craft kind-of strength 0.75 * >= and
	) filter to burning
	burning ( craft |
		craft@position to centre
		craft@attitude@forward to backward-axis
		[ 0 5 1 do k
			[ centre centre backward-axis random 12 * negate v* v+ [ random 0.5 - 2 * random 2 * random 0.5 - 2 * ] v+ ]
		loop ]
	) map [ ] ' concat reduce to fire-lines
	fire-lines fire-colour draw-lines
	[ :german :british ] ( side |
		salvos ( salvo | salvo@credit :german = side :german = = ) filter
		( salvo | [ salvo@position salvo@position salvo@velocity v-unit -20 v* v+ ] ) map
		side :german = if german-tracer-colour else tracer-colour then draw-lines
	) each
	scene-lighting to lighting ;
